###
post: Skyrme Hartree-Fock of any spherical closed-shell nucleus
agent: claude

The solver of lib/skyrme/skyrme for any nucleus whose protons and neutrons
each fill whole $(n, l, j)$ shells: oxygen-16 through lead-208, with the
forces SLy4, SLy5, SIII and SkM*.

    from skyrme.spherical import SLY5, nucleus_z, nucleus_n, solve

    res = solve(0.1, 200, SLY5, nucleus_z("208Pb"), nucleus_n("208Pb"), 0.5, 1.0e-9, 300)
    show res.e_per_a       # E/A, MeV

Two things change from lib/skyrme/skyrme, which solves oxygen-16 only.

The occupied orbitals are chosen by energy. Each iteration diagonalizes
every $(l, j)$ block up to $l = 7$, and the protons (or neutrons) go into
the lowest orbitals across all blocks, $2j + 1$ to an orbital, until all
$Z$ (or $N$) are placed. A nucleus whose last orbital would be only partly
filled is open-shell and is refused: a spherical solution with a partly
filled shell needs pairing or a filling approximation, which this solver
does not have. Inside a block the $n$-th orbital is the $n$-th eigenvalue,
so calcium-40's $2s_{1/2}$ is the second state of the $(0, 1/2)$ block.

The force and the center-of-mass factor are arguments. A force is a
Force record (SLY4, SLY5, SIII and SKMS are defined below), with a flag
for the $J^2$ terms of $t_1$ and $t_2$, which SLy5 and SIII keep and SLy4
and SkM* drop. The kinetic term carries $\hbar^2/2m \, (1 - 1/A)$ for every
force, as each was fitted.

For oxygen-16 with SLy5 the arithmetic is lib/skyrme/skyrme's, operation for
operation, and gives its bits (the test at the end).

Used with `import skyrme.spherical`.
###
from scf.loop import scf
from scf.mix import MixHistory, MixStep, broyden, linear, mix_densities, pulay
from skyrme.skyrme import E2, EIG_TOL, FOLD, HBARC, MIN_ITER, M_NUC, NEAR, NEUTRON, NKIND, PI, PROTON, WS_DIFFUSE, WS_R0, coulomb, count_below, grad1, integrate_r2, inverse_iteration, lap_r, particle_number, proton_coulomb, skyrme_o16

#| A Skyrme force: the ten parameters of the functional and whether its
#| $J^2$ terms are kept. t0 is in MeV fm^3, t1, t2 and w0 in MeV fm^5, t3 in
#| MeV fm^(3 + 3 alpha); the x's and alpha have no unit.
record Force {
    t0: Num
    t1: Num
    t2: Num
    t3: Num
    x0: Num
    x1: Num
    x2: Num
    x3: Num
    w0: Num
    alpha: Num
    j2: Bool
}

# SLy4 and SLy5: Chabanat, Bonche, Haensel, Meyer and Schaeffer, Nucl. Phys.
# A 635, 231 (1998), Table 1 (SLy5's numbers as skyrme_rpa's skyrme.in lists
# them, the same to the digits printed there)
SLY4 = Force { t0: -2488.91, t1: 486.82, t2: -546.39, t3: 13777.0, x0: 0.834, x1: -0.344, x2: -1.0, x3: 1.354, w0: 123.0, alpha: 1.0 / 6.0, j2: false }
SLY5 = Force { t0: -2484.88, t1: 483.13, t2: -549.40, t3: 13763.0, x0: 0.778, x1: -0.328, x2: -1.0, x3: 1.267, w0: 126.0, alpha: 1.0 / 6.0, j2: true }
# SIII: Beiner, Flocard, Van Giai and Quentin, Nucl. Phys. A 238, 29 (1975);
# its three-body t3 term is the density-dependent one with x3 = 1, alpha = 1
SIII = Force { t0: -1128.75, t1: 395.0, t2: -95.0, t3: 14000.0, x0: 0.45, x1: 0.0, x2: 0.0, x3: 1.0, w0: 120.0, alpha: 1.0, j2: true }
# SkM*: Bartel, Quentin, Brack, Guet and Hakansson, Nucl. Phys. A 386, 79 (1982)
SKMS = Force { t0: -2645.0, t1: 410.0, t2: -135.0, t3: 15595.0, x0: 0.09, x1: 0.0, x2: 0.0, x3: 0.0, w0: 130.0, alpha: 1.0 / 6.0, j2: false }

# ---- the blocks: l = 0 .. L_MAX, j = l + 1/2 and then (for l > 0) l - 1/2.
# L_MAX = 7 reaches 1j15/2, the first neutron shell above lead-208's 126.
L_MAX = 7
NBLOCK = 2 * L_MAX + 1
# at most this many orbitals of one block are occupied (lead-208's 3s1/2 is the third)
S_MAX = 4
# spectroscopic letters for l = 0 .. 7 (nuclear usage: j for l = 7)
L_LETTERS = "spdfghij"
# the kinds, for messages
KIND_NAMES = ["neutrons", "protons"]
# a state counts as bound below this energy, MeV
BOUND = 0.0
# the margin of the Sturm-count checks on an orbital energy, MeV
CHECK_TOL = 1.0e-7
# the element symbols, Z = 1 .. 118
ELEMENTS = split("H He Li Be B C N O F Ne Na Mg Al Si P S Cl Ar K Ca Sc Ti V Cr Mn Fe Co Ni Cu Zn Ga Ge As Se Br Kr Rb Sr Y Zr Nb Mo Tc Ru Rh Pd Ag Cd In Sn Sb Te I Xe Cs Ba La Ce Pr Nd Pm Sm Eu Gd Tb Dy Ho Er Tm Yb Lu Hf Ta W Re Os Ir Pt Au Hg Tl Pb Bi Po At Rn Fr Ra Ac Th Pa U Np Pu Am Cm Bk Cf Es Fm Md No Lr Rf Db Sg Bh Hs Mt Ds Rg Cn Nh Fl Mc Lv Ts Og", " ")

#| The l of block b; the blocks run s1/2, p3/2, p1/2, d5/2, d3/2, ...
def block_l(b) {
    if b == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    return (b + 1) // 2
}

#| The j of block b: l + 1/2 for odd b and b = 0, l - 1/2 for even b.
def block_j(b) {
    l = block_l(b)
    if b % 2 == 1 or b == 0 {
        return l + 0.5
    }
    return l - 0.5
}

#| An orbital's name: n, the letter of l, and 2j/2, as "2s1/2".
def orbital_label(n, l: Int, j) {
    return f"{n:.0f}{L_LETTERS[l]}{2.0 * j:.0f}/2"
}

#| The mass number and the proton number of a name such as "208Pb",
#| "Pb208" or "pb-208": the digits are A, the letters the element.
def nucleus_az(name: Str) {
    digits = ""
    letters = ""
    for c in name {
        if c.isdigit() {
            digits = digits + c
        }
        else if c.isalpha() {
            letters = letters + c
        }
    }
    if len(digits) == 0 or len(letters) == 0 {
        stop(f"nucleus {name!r}: write the mass number and the element, as \"208Pb\"")
    }
    sym = upper(letters[0]) + lower(letters[1:])
    z = 0
    for k to len(ELEMENTS) {
        if ELEMENTS[k] == sym {
            z = k + 1
        }
    }
    if z == 0 {
        stop(f"nucleus {name!r}: {sym!r} is not an element symbol")
    }
    a = int(digits)
    if a <= z {
        stop(f"nucleus {name!r}: the mass number {a} leaves no neutrons for Z = {z}")
    }
    return a, z
}

#| The proton number Z of a nucleus written like "208Pb".
def nucleus_z(name: Str) {
    a, z = nucleus_az(name)
    return z
}

#| The neutron number N = A - Z of a nucleus written like "208Pb".
def nucleus_n(name: Str) {
    a, z = nucleus_az(name)
    return a - z
}

#| hbar^2/2m times the one-body center-of-mass factor 1 - 1/A, MeV fm^2.
def hb_of(a) {
    return HBARC * HBARC / (2.0 * M_NUC) * (1.0 - 1.0 / a)
}

#| The mean fields of kind q from the densities: effective mass B, central U, spin-orbit W.
def fields(f: Force, hb, q, rho: Arr, tau: Arr, jso: Arr, r: Arr, h) {
    step densities {
        rt = rho[NEUTRON, :] + rho[PROTON, :]
        tt = tau[NEUTRON, :] + tau[PROTON, :]
        jt = jso[NEUTRON, :] + jso[PROTON, :]
        rq = rho[q, :]
        sj = jt + jso[q, :]
        lap_t = lap_r(rt, r, h)
        drt = grad1(rt, h)
        lap_q = lap_r(rq, r, h)
        drq = grad1(rq, h)
        dsj = grad1(sj, h)
    }
    step effective_mass {
        B = hb + 0.125 * (f.t1 * (2.0 + f.x1) + f.t2 * (2.0 + f.x2)) * rt + 0.125 * (f.t2 * (1.0 + 2.0 * f.x2) - f.t1 * (1.0 + 2.0 * f.x1)) * rq
    }
    step central {
        ra = pow(rt, f.alpha)
        U = f.t0 * ((1.0 + f.x0 / 2.0) * rt - (f.x0 + 0.5) * rq)
        U += 0.25 * f.t1 * ((1.0 + f.x1 / 2.0) * (tt - 1.5 * lap_t) - (f.x1 + 0.5) * (tau[q, :] - 1.5 * lap_q))
        U += 0.25 * f.t2 * ((1.0 + f.x2 / 2.0) * (tt + 0.5 * lap_t) + (f.x2 + 0.5) * (tau[q, :] + 0.5 * lap_q))
        rsq = rho[NEUTRON, :] * rho[NEUTRON, :] + rho[PROTON, :] * rho[PROTON, :]
        U += f.t3 / 12.0 * ((1.0 + f.x3 / 2.0) * (2.0 + f.alpha) * ra * rt - (f.x3 + 0.5) * (2.0 * ra * rq + f.alpha * ra / rt * rsq))
        U -= f.w0 * (sj / r + 0.5 * dsj)
    }
    step spin_orbit {
        W = 0.5 * f.w0 * (drt + drq)
        if f.j2 {
            W = 0.5 * f.w0 * (drt + drq) + 0.125 * (f.t1 - f.t2) * jso[q, :] - 0.125 * (f.t1 * f.x1 + f.t2 * f.x2) * jt
        }
    }
    return B, U, W
}

#| The radial Hamiltonian of one (l, j) block on the mesh, as its diagonal and off-diagonal.
def hamiltonian(B: Arr, dB: Arr, U: Arr, W: Arr, V: Arr, hb, q, l, sdl, r: Arr, h) {
    nr = len(r)
    # B halfway between neighboring points; past the last point it meets hb
    bm = copy(B)
    bm[1:nr] = 0.5 * (B[0:nr - 1] + B[1:nr])
    bp = zeros(nr) + 0.5 * (B[nr - 1] + hb)
    bp[0:nr - 1] = 0.5 * (B[0:nr - 1] + B[1:nr])
    off = -bp[0:nr - 1] / (h * h)
    diag = (bm + bp) / (h * h) + B * l * (l + 1.0) / (r * r) + dB / r + U + sdl * W / r
    if q == PROTON {
        diag = diag + V
    }
    return diag, off
}

#| The k-th lowest eigenvalue (k = 0 the lowest) of the tridiagonal matrix,
#| by bisection on the Sturm count between lo and hi, to EIG_TOL.
def kth_eigenvalue(diag: Arr, off: Arr, k, lo, hi) {
    a = lo
    b = hi
    while b - a > EIG_TOL {
        mid = 0.5 * (a + b)
        if count_below(diag, off, mid) > k {
            b = mid
        }
        else {
            a = mid
        }
    }
    return a
}

#| The total energy: the Skyrme energy density plus Coulomb, integrated over r.
def energy(f: Force, hb, rho: Arr, tau: Arr, jso: Arr, r: Arr, h) {
    rn = rho[NEUTRON, :]
    rp = rho[PROTON, :]
    rt = rn + rp
    drt = grad1(rt, h)
    drn = grad1(rn, h)
    drp = grad1(rp, h)
    tn = tau[NEUTRON, :]
    tp = tau[PROTON, :]
    tt = tn + tp
    jn = jso[NEUTRON, :]
    jp = jso[PROTON, :]
    jt = jn + jp
    rsq = rn * rn + rp * rp
    H = hb * tt + 0.5 * f.t0 * ((1.0 + f.x0 / 2.0) * rt * rt - (f.x0 + 0.5) * rsq)
    H += 0.25 * f.t1 * ((1.0 + f.x1 / 2.0) * (rt * tt + 0.75 * drt * drt) - (f.x1 + 0.5) * (rn * tn + 0.75 * drn * drn + rp * tp + 0.75 * drp * drp))
    H += 0.25 * f.t2 * ((1.0 + f.x2 / 2.0) * (rt * tt - 0.25 * drt * drt) + (f.x2 + 0.5) * (rn * tn - 0.25 * drn * drn + rp * tp - 0.25 * drp * drp))
    H += f.t3 / 12.0 * pow(rt, f.alpha) * ((1.0 + f.x3 / 2.0) * rt * rt - (f.x3 + 0.5) * rsq)
    if f.j2 {
        H += (f.t1 - f.t2) / 16.0 * (jn * jn + jp * jp) - (f.t1 * f.x1 + f.t2 * f.x2) / 16.0 * jt * jt
    }
    H += 0.5 * f.w0 * (jt * drt + jn * drn + jp * drp)
    #: Coulomb exchange in the Slater approximation
    ec = 0.5 * coulomb(rp, r, h) * rp - 0.75 * E2 * pow(3.0 / PI, 1.0 / 3.0) * pow(rp, 4.0 / 3.0)
    return integrate_r2(H, r, h) + integrate_r2(ec, r, h)
}

#| The bound states of every block of one kind, by bisection: their energies
#| (MeV), blocks and radial indices s (n = s + 1), at most S_MAX a block,
#| lowest first in each block.
def bound_states(dg: Arr, of: Arr) {
    nblk = len(dg)
    e = []
    blk = []
    idx = []
    for b to nblk {
        diag = dg[b, :]
        off = of[b, :]
        nb = min(count_below(diag, off, BOUND), S_MAX)
        # Gershgorin: every eigenvalue lies within diag[i] +- (|off[i-1]| + |off[i]|)
        big = max(abs(off))
        for s to nb {
            e = append(e, kth_eigenvalue(diag, off, s, min(diag) - 2.0 * big, max(diag) + 2.0 * big))
            blk = append(blk, b)
            idx = append(idx, s)
        }
    }
    return e, blk, idx
}

#| How many orbitals of each block hold the `want` nucleons of one kind,
#| filling the lowest orbitals across all blocks. Stops when the last
#| orbital would be partly filled (an open shell) or the bound states run out;
#| `it` is the pass, for the message.
def fill_by_energy(e: Arr, blk: Arr, want, kind: Str, it) {
    when = ""
    if it > 1 {
        when = f" In pass {round(it)} the orbitals changed order (they were closed at the start), so the iteration is running away rather than converging; lower MIX, or check the force."
    }
    #: whole shells only; a partly filled one stops the run
    occ = zeros(NBLOCK)
    placed = 0
    order = argsort(e)
    k = 0
    while placed < want {
        if k >= len(order) {
            stop(f"{kind}: only {placed} of the {want} fit in the bound orbitals; the nucleus is past the drip line or the box is too small.{when}")
        }
        b = blk[order[k]]
        deg = 2.0 * block_j(b) + 1.0
        if placed + deg > want {
            stop(f"{kind}: {want} is not a closed shell: the {orbital_label(occ[b] + 1, round(block_l(b)), block_j(b))} orbital at {e[order[k]]:.3f} MeV would hold {want - placed} of its {deg:.0f}. This solver has no pairing; give a nucleus whose protons and neutrons fill whole shells.{when}")
        }
        placed += deg
        occ[b] = occ[b] + 1
        k += 1
    }
    return occ
}

#| What solve finds: the energy per nucleon and the total energy (MeV); the
#| proton, neutron and charge radii (fm); the occupied orbitals' energies
#| (MeV, neutrons then protons, each lowest first), labels and
#| occupations; every bound orbital of the final fields with the same three;
#| the passes, whether the energy settled, how many times the occupation was
#| refilled after pass 1; the mesh (fm) and the converged number,
#| kinetic and spin-orbit densities, each `[2, nr]` (neutrons, then protons).
record Nucleus {
    z: Num
    n: Num
    e_per_a: Num
    energy: Num
    r_p: Num
    r_n: Num
    r_ch: Num
    levels: Arr
    labels: Str
    spectrum: Arr
    spectrum_labels: Str
    spectrum_occ: Arr
    iterations: Num
    converged: Bool
    refills: Num
    r: Arr
    rho: Arr
    tau: Arr
    jso: Arr
}

# ---- the radial mesh as the basis of lib/scf/loop. The densities are one
# flat array of DENSITY_ROWS rows of nr numbers: rho of the neutrons and of
# the protons, then tau, then J.

#: DENSITY_ROWS  rho, tau and J, each for the two kinds
DENSITY_ROWS: Int = 3 * round(NKIND)

#: DENSITY_FLOOR  the least number density the fields see, fm^-3. Pulay and
#:     Broyden extrapolate, and can leave the far tail of rho slightly
#:     negative before they converge, where rho^alpha is not defined. Linear
#:     mixing keeps rho positive, and on every mesh in
#:     lib/skyrme/COMPARISON.md rho stays far above the floor, so the floor
#:     changes no bit there.
DENSITY_FLOOR = 1.0e-30

#| The mesh, the force and what the iteration keeps between passes: for
#| orbital k = (q * NBLOCK + b) * S_MAX + s its vector (row k of uvec) and
#| last energy (lam[k]); how many orbitals of each block are occupied (row q
#| of occ); and the tridiagonal blocks of the kind being solved (dg, of).
#| The arrays are written in place by the functions below.
record RadialMesh {
    force: Force
    hb: Num
    h: Num
    r: Arr
    want: Arr
    uvec: Arr
    lam: Arr
    occ: Arr
    dg: Arr
    of: Arr
}

#| rho, tau and J ([NKIND, nr] each) as one flat array.
def pack_densities(rho: Arr, tau: Arr, jso: Arr) -> Arr {
    m = zeros(DENSITY_ROWS, len(rho[0, :]))
    m[0:NKIND, :] = rho
    m[NKIND:2 * NKIND, :] = tau
    m[2 * NKIND:DENSITY_ROWS, :] = jso
    return ravel(m)
}

#| rho, tau and J back from the flat array of pack_densities, rho held at
#| DENSITY_FLOOR or above.
def unpack_densities(d: Arr, nr) {
    m = reshape(d, DENSITY_ROWS, nr)
    rho = m[0:NKIND, :]
    return where(rho < DENSITY_FLOOR, DENSITY_FLOOR, rho), m[NKIND:2 * NKIND, :], m[2 * NKIND:DENSITY_ROWS, :]
}

#| Two kinds of particle: neutrons and protons.
def mesh_groups(b: RadialMesh) -> Int {
    return round(NKIND)
}

#| The (l, j) blocks of one kind.
def mesh_blocks(b: RadialMesh) -> Int {
    return round(NBLOCK)
}

#| The fields of kind q as rows B, dB/dr, U, W and the Coulomb potential V
#| (zero for neutrons).
def mesh_fields(b: RadialMesh, d: Arr, q) -> Arr {
    nr = len(b.r)
    rho, tau, jso = unpack_densities(d, nr)
    B, U, W = fields(b.force, b.hb, q, rho, tau, jso, b.r, b.h)
    f = zeros(5, nr)
    f[0, :] = B
    f[1, :] = grad1(B, b.h)
    f[2, :] = U
    f[3, :] = W
    if q == PROTON {
        f[4, :] = proton_coulomb(rho[PROTON, :], b.r, b.h)
    }
    return f
}

#| (j(j + 1) - l(l + 1) - 3/4), the spin-orbit factor of block k.
def spin_orbit_factor(k) {
    l = block_l(k)
    j = block_j(k)
    return j * (j + 1.0) - l * (l + 1.0) - 0.75
}

#| Block k of kind q, tridiagonal, kept as row k of dg and of.
def mesh_block_h(b: RadialMesh, f: Arr, q, k) -> Int {
    diag, off = hamiltonian(f[0, :], f[1, :], f[2, :], f[3, :], f[4, :], b.hb, q, block_l(k), spin_orbit_factor(k), b.r, b.h)
    b.dg[k, :] = diag
    b.of[k, :] = off
    return round(k)
}

#| The occupied orbitals of kind q. After pass 1, each from its last vector
#| by inverse iteration, shifted NEAR below its last energy; then Sturm
#| counts check that it is still the s-th state of its block and that no
#| unoccupied state fell below the highest occupied one. In pass 1, or when
#| a check fails, every bound state by bisection, filled by energy, each
#| vector from inverse iteration just below its bisected energy. Returns 1
#| when the occupation was chosen again, 0 when the check passed.
def mesh_lowest(b: RadialMesh, q, it) -> Int {
    nr = len(b.r)
    step warm {
        refill = it == 1
        if it > 1 {
            e_top = -1.0e300
            for k to NBLOCK {
                for s to b.occ[q, k] {
                    o = (q * NBLOCK + k) * S_MAX + s
                    u = b.uvec[o, :]
                    b.lam[o] = inverse_iteration(b.dg[k, :], b.of[k, :], b.lam[o] - NEAR, u)
                    b.uvec[o, :] = u
                    if count_below(b.dg[k, :], b.of[k, :], b.lam[o] - CHECK_TOL) != s or count_below(b.dg[k, :], b.of[k, :], b.lam[o] + CHECK_TOL) != s + 1 {
                        refill = true
                    }
                    e_top = max(e_top, b.lam[o])
                }
            }
            for k to NBLOCK {
                if count_below(b.dg[k, :], b.of[k, :], e_top + CHECK_TOL) != b.occ[q, k] {
                    refill = true
                }
            }
        }
    }
    step refill {
        if refill {
            be, bb, bs = bound_states(b.dg, b.of)
            b.occ[q, :] = fill_by_energy(be, bb, b.want[q], KIND_NAMES[q], it)
            for t to len(be) {
                k = bb[t]
                s = bs[t]
                if s < b.occ[q, k] {
                    o = (q * NBLOCK + k) * S_MAX + s
                    u = zeros(nr) + 1.0
                    b.lam[o] = inverse_iteration(b.dg[k, :], b.of[k, :], be[t] - EIG_TOL, u)
                    b.uvec[o, :] = u
                }
            }
        }
    }
    changed: Int = 0
    if refill {
        changed = 1
    }
    return changed
}

#| The densities of kind q's occupied orbitals, added into d_out: rho,
#| tau = |dR/dr|^2 + l(l + 1)/r^2 R^2 and J = (j(j + 1) - l(l + 1) - 3/4)/r R^2,
#| each weighted by (2j + 1)/4 pi.
def mesh_add_densities(b: RadialMesh, q, d_out: Arr) -> Arr {
    nr = len(b.r)
    r = b.r
    h = b.h
    at_rho = q * nr
    at_tau = (NKIND + q) * nr
    at_jso = (2 * NKIND + q) * nr
    for k to NBLOCK {
        l = block_l(k)
        j = block_j(k)
        sdl = spin_orbit_factor(k)
        for s to b.occ[q, k] {
            o = (q * NBLOCK + k) * S_MAX + s
            R = b.uvec[o, :] / (sqrt(h) * r)
            dR = grad1(R, h)
            wt = (2.0 * j + 1.0) / (4.0 * PI)
            d_out[at_rho:at_rho + nr] = d_out[at_rho:at_rho + nr] + wt * R * R
            d_out[at_tau:at_tau + nr] = d_out[at_tau:at_tau + nr] + wt * (dR * dR + l * (l + 1.0) / (r * r) * R * R)
            d_out[at_jso:at_jso + nr] = d_out[at_jso:at_jso + nr] + wt * sdl / r * R * R
        }
    }
    return d_out
}

#| The total energy of the packed densities d.
def mesh_energy(b: RadialMesh, d: Arr) -> Num {
    rho, tau, jso = unpack_densities(d, len(b.r))
    return energy(b.force, b.hb, rho, tau, jso, b.r, b.h)
}

#| Linear mixing with the fraction alpha, as one step of lib/scf/mix.
def linear_step(x_in: Arr, x_out: Arr, hist: MixHistory, alpha) -> MixStep {
    x, hs, res = linear(x_in, x_out, hist, alpha = alpha)
    return MixStep { x: x, hist: hs, residual: res }
}

#| Spherical Skyrme-Hartree-Fock of a closed-shell nucleus, densities mixed
#| linearly with the fraction `mix` until the energy settles.
def solve(h, nr, force: Force, z, n, mix, e_tol, max_iter) -> Nucleus {
    return solve_with(h, nr, force, z, n, fn(x_in, x_out, hist) -> linear_step(x_in, x_out, hist, mix), e_tol, max_iter)
}

#| Spherical Skyrme-Hartree-Fock of a closed-shell nucleus on the radial
#| mesh, by lib/scf/loop, with the densities mixed by `mixer`, a function
#| (x_in, x_out, hist) -> MixStep (lib/scf/mix).
def solve_with(h, nr, force: Force, z, n, mixer, e_tol, max_iter) -> Nucleus {
    a_nuc = z + n
    hb = hb_of(a_nuc)
    kind_tag = ["n", "p"]
    nst = NBLOCK * S_MAX
    step mesh {
        r = zeros(nr)
        for i to nr {
            r[i] = (i + 1) * h
        }
    }
    step start {
        # a Woods-Saxon profile holding N neutrons and Z protons
        rho = zeros(NKIND, nr)
        prof = 1.0 / (1.0 + exp((r - WS_R0 * pow(a_nuc, 1.0 / 3.0)) / WS_DIFFUSE))
        pn = integrate_r2(prof, r, h)
        rho[NEUTRON, :] = prof * n / pn
        rho[PROTON, :] = prof * z / pn
        d0 = pack_densities(rho, zeros(NKIND, nr), zeros(NKIND, nr))
        basis = RadialMesh { force: force, hb: hb, h: h, r: r, want: [n, z], uvec: zeros(NKIND * nst, nr) + 1.0, lam: zeros(NKIND * nst), occ: zeros(NKIND, NBLOCK), dg: zeros(NBLOCK, nr), of: zeros(NBLOCK, nr - 1) }
    }
    run = scf(basis, d0, mesh_groups, mesh_blocks, mesh_fields, mesh_block_h, mesh_lowest, mesh_add_densities, mesh_energy, mixer, e_tol, round(max_iter), round(MIN_ITER))
    rho, tau, jso = unpack_densities(run.d, nr)
    occ = basis.occ
    lam = basis.lam
    dg = basis.dg
    of = basis.of
    E = run.energy
    V = zeros(nr)
    step levels {
        # the occupied orbitals, each kind lowest first
        levels = []
        labels = ""
        for q to NKIND {
            ql = []
            qn = []
            for b to NBLOCK {
                for s to occ[q, b] {
                    ql = append(ql, lam[(q * NBLOCK + b) * S_MAX + s])
                    qn = append(qn, b * S_MAX + s)
                }
            }
            for t in argsort(ql) {
                b = qn[t] // S_MAX
                s = qn[t] - b * S_MAX
                levels = append(levels, ql[t])
                labels = labels + ("," if len(labels) > 0 else "") + kind_tag[q] + " " + orbital_label(s + 1, round(block_l(b)), block_j(b))
            }
        }
    }
    step spectrum {
        # every bound orbital of the last fields (the ones the last pass
        # diagonalized), by bisection, with its occupation
        spectrum = []
        spectrum_occ = []
        spectrum_labels = ""
        for q to NKIND {
            B, U, W = fields(force, hb, q, rho, tau, jso, r, h)
            dB = grad1(B, h)
            if q == PROTON {
                V = proton_coulomb(rho[PROTON, :], r, h)
            }
            for b to NBLOCK {
                l = block_l(b)
                j = block_j(b)
                sdl = j * (j + 1.0) - l * (l + 1.0) - 0.75
                diag, off = hamiltonian(B, dB, U, W, V, hb, q, l, sdl, r, h)
                dg[b, :] = diag
                of[b, :] = off
            }
            be, bb, bs = bound_states(dg, of)
            for t in argsort(be) {
                b = bb[t]
                spectrum = append(spectrum, be[t])
                spectrum_occ = append(spectrum_occ, (2.0 * block_j(b) + 1.0) if bs[t] < occ[q, b] else 0.0)
                spectrum_labels = spectrum_labels + ("," if len(spectrum_labels) > 0 else "") + kind_tag[q] + " " + orbital_label(bs[t] + 1, round(block_l(b)), block_j(b))
            }
        }
    }
    step observables {
        r2p = integrate_r2(rho[PROTON, :] * r * r, r, h) / z
        r2n = integrate_r2(rho[NEUTRON, :] * r * r, r, h) / n
    }
    return Nucleus { z: z, n: n, e_per_a: E / a_nuc, energy: E, r_p: sqrt(r2p), r_n: sqrt(r2n), r_ch: sqrt(r2p + 1.5 * FOLD * FOLD), levels: levels, labels: labels, spectrum: spectrum, spectrum_labels: spectrum_labels, spectrum_occ: spectrum_occ, iterations: run.passes, converged: run.converged, refills: run.refills, r: r, rho: rho, tau: tau, jso: jso }
}

# ---- tests
SP_H = 0.1
SP_BOX = 15.0

test "the element table puts oxygen at 8, calcium at 20, tin at 50 and lead at 82" {
    assert_near(nucleus_z("16O"), 8, 0.0)
    assert_near(nucleus_z("ca40"), 20, 0.0)
    assert_near(nucleus_n("Sn-132"), 82, 0.0)
    assert_near(nucleus_z("208Pb"), 82, 0.0)
    assert_near(len(ELEMENTS), 118, 0.0)
    assert_true(ELEMENTS[117] == "Og")
}

test "the blocks run 1/2+, 3/2-, 1/2-, 5/2+, 3/2+, ... up to l = 7" {
    assert_near(block_l(0), 0, 0.0)
    assert_near(block_j(0), 0.5, 0.0)
    assert_near(block_j(1), 1.5, 0.0)
    assert_near(block_j(2), 0.5, 0.0)
    assert_near(block_l(NBLOCK - 1), L_MAX, 0.0)
    assert_true(orbital_label(1, 6, 6.5) == "1i13/2")
}

test "oxygen-16 with SLy5 gives lib/skyrme/skyrme's bits" {
    sp_old = skyrme_o16(SP_H, round(SP_BOX / SP_H))
    sp_new = solve(SP_H, round(SP_BOX / SP_H), SLY5, 8, 8, 0.5, 1.0e-9, 300)
    assert_near(sp_new.energy, sp_old.energy, 0.0)
    assert_near(sp_new.r_ch, sp_old.r_ch, 0.0)
    assert_near(max(abs(sp_new.levels - sp_old.levels)), 0.0, 0.0)
    assert_near(sp_new.iterations, sp_old.iterations, 0.0)
    assert_true(sp_new.labels == "n 1s1/2,n 1p3/2,n 1p1/2,p 1s1/2,p 1p3/2,p 1p1/2")
}

#: SP_TIGHT  a tolerance on the energy far below where the three mixers
#:     stop differing, MeV
SP_TIGHT = 1.0e-13
#: SP_AGREE_E  how closely the mixers' converged E/A agree, MeV; the
#:     largest difference seen is 2e-14 (calcium-40, oxygen-16)
SP_AGREE_E = 1.0e-12
#: SP_AGREE_RHO  how closely their converged densities agree, fm^-3; the
#:     largest difference seen is 5e-13
SP_AGREE_RHO = 1.0e-11
#: SP_ITER  a cap on passes no mixer reaches here
SP_ITER = 1000

#| Mixing steps by each method of mix_densities, for the test below.
def sp_linear(x_in: Arr, x_out: Arr, hist: MixHistory) -> MixStep {
    x, hs, res = mix_densities(x_in, x_out, hist) using linear
    return MixStep { x: x, hist: hs, residual: res }
}
def sp_pulay(x_in: Arr, x_out: Arr, hist: MixHistory) -> MixStep {
    x, hs, res = mix_densities(x_in, x_out, hist) using pulay
    return MixStep { x: x, hist: hs, residual: res }
}
def sp_broyden(x_in: Arr, x_out: Arr, hist: MixHistory) -> MixStep {
    x, hs, res = mix_densities(x_in, x_out, hist) using broyden
    return MixStep { x: x, hist: hs, residual: res }
}

# mix_densities has no per-call agreement on the densities (two mixers
# make different next densities on purpose), so its methods are compared
# here, where they should agree: at the converged ground state
test "linear, Pulay and Broyden mixing reach the same oxygen-16, Pulay and Broyden in fewer passes" {
    nr: Int = round(SP_BOX / SP_H)
    by_lin = solve_with(SP_H, nr, SLY4, 8, 8, sp_linear, SP_TIGHT, SP_ITER)
    by_pul = solve_with(SP_H, nr, SLY4, 8, 8, sp_pulay, SP_TIGHT, SP_ITER)
    by_bro = solve_with(SP_H, nr, SLY4, 8, 8, sp_broyden, SP_TIGHT, SP_ITER)
    assert_true(by_lin.converged and by_pul.converged and by_bro.converged)
    assert_near(by_pul.e_per_a, by_lin.e_per_a, SP_AGREE_E)
    assert_near(by_bro.e_per_a, by_lin.e_per_a, SP_AGREE_E)
    assert_near(max(abs(by_pul.rho - by_lin.rho)), 0.0, SP_AGREE_RHO)
    assert_near(max(abs(by_bro.rho - by_lin.rho)), 0.0, SP_AGREE_RHO)
    assert_true(by_pul.labels == by_lin.labels and by_bro.labels == by_lin.labels)
    assert_true(by_pul.iterations < by_lin.iterations and by_bro.iterations < by_lin.iterations)
}

